---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Lineage, provenance and verification"
  description="Trace how the PDTF 1.0-derived ontology was sourced and decided, inspect its historical modelling record, and independently verify its correspondence with the PDTF JSON Schema."
>
  <PageMeta category="PDTF 1.0 · extracted ontology" variant="brand" updated="Draft · under review" />
  <h1>Lineage, provenance and verification</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Use this category to follow the extracted ontology back to its PDTF 1.0 sources,
    understand the recorded modelling path, and inspect the separate checks that test the
    schema–ontology correspondence. These are related forms of traceability, but they are
    not interchangeable.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--warn">
    <p class="callout__label">PDTF 1.0-derived draft</p>
    <p>
      This category documents a draft semantic corpus derived from PDTF 1.0. It is not an
      approved SPDTF 2.0 ontology. Each source, decision, historical record and verification
      artefact keeps the maturity and authority stated on its own page.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="three-traces">Three different traces</h2>
  <table>
    <caption>What each trace establishes and what it does not</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Trace</th><th scope="col">Question answered</th><th scope="col">Boundary</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Source and decision provenance</th>
        <td>Where did a term come from, and which ODR, ADR or council record governed the modelling choice?</td>
        <td>A citation records lineage; it does not prove complete schema coverage.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">Historical modelling record</th>
        <td>Which standards, bounded contexts, taxonomy, OWL, SHACL and JSON-LD approaches were explored?</td>
        <td>The record contains mixed-maturity work and explicitly retained stubs.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th scope="row">RML verification bridge</th>
        <td>Do cited schema locations and ontology terms resolve in both directions?</td>
        <td><strong>RML is an independent bidirectional verification bridge, not a derivation step or runtime ETL pipeline.</strong></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="follow">Follow the evidence</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard
      href="/pdtf-1/extracted-ontology/lineage-provenance-and-verification/decision-provenance"
      title="Decision provenance"
      eyebrow="Source and decisions"
      description="Use the full ODR, ADR and council corpus to trace term-level dct:source citations, the decisions governing every layer, retirement and reconciliation."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/pdtf-1/extracted-ontology/lineage-provenance-and-verification/historical-modelling"
      title="Historical modelling record"
      eyebrow="Recorded method"
      description="Review the standards stack, bounded-context work and retained taxonomy, OWL, SHACL and JSON-LD design records with their original maturity labels."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/pdtf-1/extracted-ontology/lineage-provenance-and-verification/schema-to-ontology-verification"
      title="RML schema–ontology verification"
      eyebrow="Independent check"
      description="Inspect the machine-checked bidirectional bridge: 466 of 469 domain-module resources (99.4%) traced to PDTF 1.0 schema origins as an independent check alongside dct:source."
    />
    <GatewayCard
      href="/pdtf-1/original-standard"
      title="Original PDTF 1.0 standard"
      eyebrow="Source corpus"
      description="Return to the JSON Schemas, overlays, dictionary, glossary and implementation material from which the semantic corpus was derived."
    />
  </div>

  <h2 id="reading-order">A defensible reading order</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Start with provenance to identify the stated source and governing decision.</li>
    <li>Use the historical record to understand why a modelling approach was proposed or retained.</li>
    <li>Use the RML coverage and validation pages to test correspondence independently.</li>
    <li>Carry forward the page-level status; traceability does not promote a draft artefact.</li>
  </ol>
</Layout>
